WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.370
A letter for me?

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.870
Yeah. It says it’s from
the Isshu Region!

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.430
Isshu?!

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.840
Thanks, Negigaknight!

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.870
Oh, Pikachu!
It’s from Iris.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.100
Who?

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.250
She’s a friend from
when I traveled through Isshu.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.980
She’s training to be a Dragon Master.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.800
She says
“Let’s have an official battle!”

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:56.030
Looks like Iris entered the Championships recently,
and she’s in the Super Class!

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:59.220
Ooh! A showdown between
traveling companions!

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.090
Yeah!

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.960
Isn’t that exciting, Pikachu?!

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:45.310
Satoshi’s friend Iris
invited him to battle her.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:49.220
Satoshi and Go immediately
flew to Isshu,

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:49.560
to meet Iris in Soryu City.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.150
Soryu City, Isshu Region
to meet Iris in Soryu City.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:52.810
Soryu City, Isshu Region

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.530
Of course,
Go made the most of his return to Isshu...

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:59.150
Monster Ball, go! Go!

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:05.540
Baope and Hiyape’s data
will be added to the Index!

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.900
Okay, now I just need Yanape.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.760
Right. Monster Ball, go!

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.370
Owwwww!

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.510
A person?!

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.010
Ugh... Who did that?

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:25.860
Oh, sorry.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.890
I just thought you
were a Pokémon...

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.480
Well, I guess you don’t often
find people napping in trees...

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.860
Wait, I overslept!

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.570
Thanks for waking me up!

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:41.670
Maybe that <i>was</i> a Pokémon...

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:48.540
Soryu Gym...
I haven’t been here in a while!

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.160
Oh, Kibago!

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.990
You think it’s Iris’s?

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:58.270
Ahh... Satoshi,
it’s nice to see you.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:03:59.950
Mr. Shaga!

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.690
Is that Iris’s Kibago?

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:04.680
No, this one is my partner.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.560
Iris is waiting for you inside.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.300
Thanks for letting us
use the Gym today!

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.690
Satoshi!

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.060
Oh, Go! How’d it go?
Catch anything?

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.970
Yeah, it was great!

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:19.860
Though I mistook a girl for a Pokémon...

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:20.850
Huh?

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:24.290
Mr. Shaga, this is my friend Go
and his Sarunori.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.450
Oh, hello.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:28.760
I am Soryu Gym’s
Gym Leader, Shaga.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.970
Shaga, Gym Leader and
Headmaster of Soryu Academy.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.850
He is also Iris’s mentor.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.300
This is an official
battle announcement.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.700
Oh, here it is!

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.430
It would seem she’s ready.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.280
Hey! Iris!

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:53.980
Huh?

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:02.820
Emonga!

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.410
I’ve been waiting for this, Satoshi!

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:13.330
Iris?!

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:16.160
What’s with the outfit?

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:18.990
Pretty, right?

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:23.600
Iris is currently
the Isshu Region’s top trainer.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:27.340
In other words,
she is our reigning Champion.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:34.270
You’re that...

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.230
Oh, you guys!

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:41.230
Hi! Sorry about earlier...

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.630
Don’t sweat it!

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.570
Iris!
I haven’t seen you in so long!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.210
Ooh, Pikachu!

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:50.870
You’re still so soft!

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:58.570
So? Whaddaya think?

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:01.460
I’m the Champion of Isshu!
Was that a shock?

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.340
Yeah! It was!

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:07.000
All right!
My surprise worked perfectly!

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.920
So this is Iris...?

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:12.470
Since her journey with Satoshi,

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:15.580
Iris has battled Dragon trainers
from far and wide,

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:18.520
and continued to meet and
learn about Dragon Pokémon.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:23.270
With belief in her Pokémon,
she has risen to become Champion.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:24.820
Huh...

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:28.740
I don’t think I’ve reached my goal,
even if I am the Champion.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.780
I’m still not a Dragon Master,
anyway!

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:35.830
I’ve wanted to keep testing myself,
so that’s why I entered the Championships!

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.030
A battle with
Isshu’s Champion...

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.580
I couldn’t ask for
a better opponent!

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:40.830
I’m getting fired up!

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.630
I knew it!
I thought you’d say that.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:46.370
Soon as someone talks about battling,
you’re raring to go.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:48.690
You’re such a kid about it.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.240
Hey, you’re a kid too!

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:53.270
Hey, I’m no kid!
I’m the <i>Champion</i>, y’know!

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:57.910
You two...
Weren’t you about to battle?

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.350
Ahh! I’m sorry, Sir!

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.650
Now, Satoshi!
Try and take on my Dragon Army!

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:04.230
Yeah!

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.690
I’ll fight dragons with dragons!

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:12.010
It’s so cute!

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.200
Satoshi, you caught a Kairyu?!

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:16.450
It’s so soft and squishy...

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.130
It’s going to be a Dragon battle?!

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:25.040
Soryu Gym is a Dragon-type Gym.
It’s a fitting choice for a battle here.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.920
So there you go, Pikachu.
Cheer me on, though, okay?

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.020
Huh? What’s going on?

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:41.210
Iris can understand
the feelings of Dragon Pokémon.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:42.270
Whaa—?!

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:51.680
It’s really kind, isn’t it?

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.690
Yeah! And strong!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.330
Wow... She’s right!

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:00.580
Let’s do our best. Both of us.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.190
Ah!

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:10.920
Looks like it’s been
waiting all this time.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:16.410
The Pokémon World Championships
has approved this Super Class battle!

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:21.160
The match-up is Contestant Satoshi
VS Contestant Iris.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:24.060
I’m gonna beat you and
make my ranking shoot up!

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.720
My ticket to the Hyper Class
is on the line here!

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.020
I’m not gonna lose!

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:32.240
This battle will be a 2v2.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:35.870
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:37.260
3!

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:38.230
2!

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:38.990
1!

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.200
Go!

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.490
Kairyu! I choose you!

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.880
Go! Kairyu!

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:56.930
Don’t worry.
He’s nice, even if he doesn’t look it.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.680
You say that, but that stare
is <i>really</i> creepy...

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:08.060
Satoshi! I’ve been super looking forward
to our battle today!

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.690
Yeah! Me, too!

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.910
If I battle with you,

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:17.150
not only will I get stronger,
my Pokémon will, too!

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.820
And we’ll get to
know each other even better!

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.200
Let’s give this all we’ve got, Iris!

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.160
Okay, Satoshi!

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.080
Battle, start!

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.330
Let’s go! Dragon Dive!

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:32.090
Kairyu! Destroyer Beam!

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.510
Pocket Monsters!

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.940
You okay, Kairyu?

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:16.000
They struck immediately...

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:20.620
That Kairyu has been a brawler
since before she caught him.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:26.560
Working in harmony with Iris
has only honed his battle sense.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.890
Let’s go! Dragon Claw!

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:32.350
Now, that’s more like it!
Thunder Punch!

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:41.700
Hurricane!

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.830
You’ve got it!
Keep it up, Kairyu!

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.460
Ice Beam!

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.130
Blow it away with Hurricane!

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:58.890
Yow!

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.960
Whoops...

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.520
Don’t worry about it.
Continue the battle.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.860
Kairyu! Dragon Dive!

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.450
Counter it! Dragon Claw!

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:28.540
Kairyu!

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.320
It really is fast...

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:52.190
Return for now, Kairyu.

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:57.150
That was close...

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.900
What do you think?
This is how a Champion battles!

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:02.260
I’m not giving up yet!

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:04.910
Uonoragon! I choose you!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:10.550
Hey, wait, hold on!
We’re in the middle of a battle!

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.920
That’s a Dragon type?!

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:17.420
No way!
Pokémon can’t be <i>that</i> cute!

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:20.960
Apparently it’s a new species
discovered in the Galar region.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:22.680
I haven’t seen one before, either.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:26.320
So you’re Uonoragon?
You’re so charming!

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:27.430
Uonoragon!

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:29.220
Let’s battle!

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.980
Kairyu! Dragon Dive!

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.110
Jaw Bite!

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.360
Whaaat?!

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.360
All right!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.660
What’s this?

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:43.780
Whoa...

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:46.490
Thunder Punch!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.830
What’s wrong?!
Use Thunder Punch!

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:54.580
His head’s jammed in its mouth,
so he can’t hear her commands...!

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:55.780
Ice Fang!

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.300
No way!

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.630
Good work, Uonoragon!
Spit him out!

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:12.510
Kairyu is unable to battle!

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:14.090
Come back, Kairyu!

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:20.630
He really threw off our pace...

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:23.810
But... I’ll hone my mind
and become one with my Pokémon!

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:26.070
Go, my trump card!

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:30.970
This is Ononox!

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:36.500
Ononox! Axe Jaw Pokémon!
Dragon type!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:41.500
Its resilient tusks can even slice through
thick, sturdy steel columns!

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.830
Iris!

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:46.630
That Ononox...
Did your Kibago evolve?!

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:50.760
Yeah! He’s risen to become
my strongest partner!

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:56.890
Is that right...?
He’s really grown!

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.150
Now, Ononox! Dragon Pulse!

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:03.900
Water Gun!

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:11.490
Uonoragon...

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:12.620
Psycho Cutter!

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:23.090
Uonoragon is unable to battle!

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.660
He’s strong...

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.470
Return, Uonoragon!

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:34.140
Thank you.
You gave it all you had.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:36.730
Kairyu gave us a hint!

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:39.850
”Beware of its mouth!”

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:42.600
I can’t risk getting close
to Uonoragon.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:45.610
And so I finished it off
from a distance!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.130
Now that’s the Iris I remember!

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:49.840
But the match isn’t <i>finished</i> just yet!

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:51.280
I’m counting on you, Kairyu!

00:14:55.790 --> 00:15:01.450
Ononox is still unharmed,
but Kairyu is still damaged from the previous battle.

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:03.920
Satoshi’s in quite the pinch...

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.800
Now! Dragon Dance!

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:13.360
Then follow it up with
Dragon Claw!

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:16.060
Ononox! Reversed Scale!

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.100
Kairyu!

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:36.410
Satoshi! After rampaging
with Reversed Scale, it’ll be confused!

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.430
Now’s the best time
to strike back!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.040
Kairyu...

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:01.850
It’s not confused...

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:05.110
Heheh!
Isn’t my Ononox awesome?

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:09.270
He hit his own head
when attacking, remember?

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.490
That shook off the confusion!

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:14.740
That way you can’t take him out
while he’s confused!

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:19.930
That’s possible...?

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:23.000
It’s the fruit of
their hard work together.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:36.090
Kairyu! We’re not gonna give up!
We can still do this!

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.100
That’s right!
We’ll show you how <i>we</i> battle!

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:46.360
Kairyu...

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:52.860
Iris...

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:56.370
Is that the thing from before...?

00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:00.910
Kairyu... You should relax more.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:08.850
Kairyu...
You really love Satoshi, don’t you?

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:11.260
That’s why you
try so hard for him.

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:16.340
You’re really kind.

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:21.650
Back when my Ononox was a Kibago,
he was kind, and a little shy, too.

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:28.310
But as he learned more and more moves,
he found battling more and more fun!

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:32.530
And when he’s having fun,
I’m having fun, too!

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:36.590
So you should
have fun battling, too!

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:39.150
If you do that,
Satoshi’ll have fun, too!

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.630
That’s it!
You’ve got it, Kairyu!

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:58.010
Kairyu... Did you talk about
something with Iris?

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:02.260
It’s a secret!

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.140
You’re good to go, then?

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:11.020
Let’s go for it! Wide Breaker!

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:14.500
Dragon Claw!

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:22.080
Psycho Cutter!

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.870
Kairyu! Use Hurricane on yourself!

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:26.870
On itself?!

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:29.250
He’s come up with something!

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:38.050
All right...!

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:40.590
He used Hurricane as a barrier?

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.430
This is how Satoshi battles!

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.330
You’re having fun now,
right, Kairyu?!

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:49.940
Go on, get really excited!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.060
Why’s she cheering <i>us</i> on?!

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:55.070
I wanna show Kairyu
how fun battling can be!

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:56.820
Because I want our battle
to heat up even more!

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:59.490
Then I’ll show you
what a heated attack looks like!

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:00.860
Keep building up the Hurricane!

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:06.500
Dragon Pulse!

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.580
Swallow it up with Hurricane!

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:31.630
Kairyu’s power can
affect the weather at times.

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:33.480
But to alter it this much...

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:39.860
I’ve got your Dragon Pulse!

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:41.060
What?

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:43.700
Th-That’s...

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:45.450
What?

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:48.810
Incredible.

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:53.000
They took on the energy from the Dragon Pulse,
and used it for a new move!

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:54.960
But that means... No way!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.800
Go! Draco Meteor!

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:06.260
Reversed Scale!

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:26.450
Ononox is unable to battle!
Kairyu wins!

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:29.320
As such, the winner is
Contestant Satoshi!

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.500
We did it, Kairyu!

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.090
That was an
amazing battle, Satoshi!

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:40.170
Based on the results of this battle,

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:44.800
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:49.810
Thank you, Ononox.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:52.980
Let’s keep working hard,
together.

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:56.810
This battle between
Dragon Pokémon...

00:20:56.810 --> 00:21:00.120
...was truly complex and impactful.

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:01.320
Sir...

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:04.320
Still... I lost.

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:08.450
Oh! 99th!

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:10.930
I got into the Hyper Class!

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.330
Keep up that momentum
and go-go, yeah!

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:17.580
Congratulations, Satoshi.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:19.460
Iris...

00:21:19.890 --> 00:21:21.070
Thanks!

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:26.700
We’ll make it to the Hyper Class soon enough,
so wait for us, okay?

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:28.960
Yeah. Let’s battle again sometime!

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:31.180
Best wishes! It’s a promise!

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:37.740
Emerging victorious from his fierce fight with Iris,
Satoshi has finally risen to a new class.

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:42.320
